<main id="main">

<section class="ls-hero"><div class="ls-w ls-hero-g"><div class="ls-hero-t"><p class="ls-ey">Lesson one</p><h1><span class="ls-hl">Learn it once.</span><br><span class="ls-hl ls-hl2">Remember it for good.</span></h1><svg class="ls-ul" viewBox="0 0 400 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 14 Q100 2 200 12 T396 8"/></svg><p class="ls-hero-p">An independent guide to studying well: the methods that research shows actually work, and simple tools to practise them today.</p><div class="ls-hero-a"><a class="ls-btn" href="#curve">See the forgetting curve</a><a class="ls-ln" href="study-methods-guide.html">Read the methods</a></div></div><div class="ls-hero-v"><div class="ls-pol rv rv-z"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1641203251058-3eb0ad540780?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=680&q=75" alt="a person sitting at a desk writing on paper" width="560" height="680" fetchpriority="high"><span>study session, 4:15&nbsp;pm</span></div><div class="ls-note" aria-hidden="true">Remember:<br>test, space, mix!</div></div></div></section>

<section class="ls-s ls-band"><div class="ls-band-i pxw"><img data-px=".14" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1568667256549-094345857637?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1800&h=800&q=75" alt="a wooden bookshelf full of books" width="1800" height="800" loading="lazy"></div><div class="ls-w ls-band-g stg"><div class="rv"><b data-count="50">50</b><small>%</small><span>of new information can fade within a day without review</span></div><div class="rv"><b data-count="4">4</b><span>well-spaced reviews to make most facts last</span></div><div class="rv"><b data-count="25">25</b><small>min</small><span>a focused study block, then a short break</span></div></div></section>

<section class="ls-s ls-cv" id="curve"><div class="ls-w ls-cv-g"><div><p class="ls-ey">Worksheet 1</p><h2 class="rv">The forgetting curve</h2><p class="ls-p">Memory fades fast, then slower. Every review lifts it back up and makes it fade more slowly. Tap the days to schedule your reviews.</p><div class="ls-days" id="cv-d" role="group" aria-label="Review days"></div><p class="ls-cv-o" id="cv-o" aria-live="polite"></p></div><div class="ls-paper"><svg viewBox="0 0 520 320" id="cv-svg" aria-hidden="true"></svg></div></div></section>

<section class="ls-s ls-acc-s"><div class="ls-w"><p class="ls-ey">The five rooms of learning</p><h2 class="rv">Walk through the methods</h2></div><div class="ls-w ls-acc"><div class="ls-acc-p on" tabindex="0"><div class="ls-acc-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1711062717294-8902df8cebe3?auto=format&fit=crop&w=900&h=1100&q=75" alt="chalk sticks on the ledge of a blackboard" width="900" height="1100" loading="lazy"></div><div class="ls-acc-t"><span>01</span><h3>Retrieval</h3><p>Close the book and recall. Effortful recall is what makes memory stick.</p></div></div><div class="ls-acc-p" tabindex="0"><div class="ls-acc-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1723877896976-2526130e50c8?auto=format&fit=crop&w=900&h=1100&q=75" alt="an empty classroom with a blackboard" width="900" height="1100" loading="lazy"></div><div class="ls-acc-t"><span>02</span><h3>Spacing</h3><p>Short sessions spread over days beat one long session the night before.</p></div></div><div class="ls-acc-p" tabindex="0"><div class="ls-acc-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1719159381962-4170890ada4e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=900&h=1100&q=75" alt="a classroom with rows of wooden desks" width="900" height="1100" loading="lazy"></div><div class="ls-acc-t"><span>03</span><h3>Interleaving</h3><p>Mix related topics in one session so you learn to tell them apart.</p></div></div><div class="ls-acc-p" tabindex="0"><div class="ls-acc-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1763098844157-d0fffcc966a1?auto=format&fit=crop&w=900&h=1100&q=75" alt="sunlight streaming into an empty classroom" width="900" height="1100" loading="lazy"></div><div class="ls-acc-t"><span>04</span><h3>Elaboration</h3><p>Ask why and how. Connect new ideas to what you already know.</p></div></div><div class="ls-acc-p" tabindex="0"><div class="ls-acc-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1641683521844-700c456379bd?auto=format&fit=crop&w=900&h=1100&q=75" alt="a man writing on a chalkboard in front of a class" width="900" height="1100" loading="lazy"></div><div class="ls-acc-t"><span>05</span><h3>Teaching</h3><p>Explain it to someone else. Gaps in your understanding appear at once.</p></div></div></div></section>

<section class="ls-s ls-fcs"><div class="ls-w"><div class="ls-cen"><p class="ls-ey">Worksheet 2</p><h2 class="rv">Flash cards for your brain</h2><p class="ls-p">Five study habits on five index cards. Try to recall each one before you flip it. That is retrieval practice already.</p></div><div class="ls-fc-g stg"><div class="ls-fc" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Flip card: Retrieval practice"><div class="ls-fc-in"><div class="ls-fc-f"><span>Card 1</span><b>Retrieval practice</b><i>Tap to flip</i></div><div class="ls-fc-b"><p>Test yourself before you feel ready. Flashcards, blank-page recall and past questions all count.</p></div></div></div><div class="ls-fc" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Flip card: Spaced repetition"><div class="ls-fc-in"><div class="ls-fc-f"><span>Card 2</span><b>Spaced repetition</b><i>Tap to flip</i></div><div class="ls-fc-b"><p>Review just as you are about to forget: after a day, then three days, then a week.</p></div></div></div><div class="ls-fc" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Flip card: Interleaving"><div class="ls-fc-in"><div class="ls-fc-f"><span>Card 3</span><b>Interleaving</b><i>Tap to flip</i></div><div class="ls-fc-b"><p>Mix problem types instead of doing twenty of the same kind in a row.</p></div></div></div><div class="ls-fc" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Flip card: Dual coding"><div class="ls-fc-in"><div class="ls-fc-f"><span>Card 4</span><b>Dual coding</b><i>Tap to flip</i></div><div class="ls-fc-b"><p>Pair words with pictures: a diagram, a timeline or a sketch beside your notes.</p></div></div></div><div class="ls-fc" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Flip card: Concrete examples"><div class="ls-fc-in"><div class="ls-fc-f"><span>Card 5</span><b>Concrete examples</b><i>Tap to flip</i></div><div class="ls-fc-b"><p>Anchor every abstract idea to a real, specific example you can picture.</p></div></div></div></div></div></section>

<section class="ls-s ls-tm" id="timer"><div class="ls-w ls-tm-g"><div class="ls-tm-c"><svg viewBox="0 0 240 240" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="120" cy="120" r="104" class="tr"/><circle cx="120" cy="120" r="104" class="tp" id="tm-p" pathLength="100"/></svg><div class="ls-tm-v"><b id="tm-t">25:00</b><span id="tm-m">Focus</span></div></div><div><p class="ls-ey">Worksheet 3</p><h2 class="rv">The study timer</h2><p class="ls-p">Work in focused blocks with short breaks. Choose a length, press start and put your phone in another room.</p><div class="ls-chips" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Session length"><label><input type="radio" name="tl" value="25" checked><span>25 / 5</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="tl" value="45"><span>45 / 10</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="tl" value="15"><span>15 / 3</span></label></div><div class="ls-tm-b"><button type="button" class="ls-btn" id="tm-go">Start</button><button type="button" class="ls-btn ls-btn2" id="tm-rs">Reset</button></div><p class="ls-tm-o" id="tm-o" aria-live="polite">Sessions completed today: <b id="tm-n">0</b></p></div></div></section>

